{{/* Written once per machine at `chezmoi init`. It asks NOTHING.

     Mate's call, 2026-08-30: "don't ask any questions whatsoever. Just ask if it's Windows
     or Mac." The platform question belongs in the browser prompt, before any of this
     exists, because that is the one place the two paths genuinely differ (WSL). By the
     time this file runs, `uname` already knows.

     Removing the last two prompts is not just less friction — it changes what is possible.
     chezmoi's prompts need a TTY, which is why the agent could not run the installer.
     With no prompts there is no TTY requirement, so the agent runs the whole thing and the
     person pastes one line and watches. It also means the install command never has to
     appear inside prompts/setup.md, which is capped at 60 columns by the website's build
     and could not have held it.

     The two answers that used to be questions now live in .chezmoidata.yaml. */}}
sourceDir = "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/projects/piy-genie"
